---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Mosses Sketchbook - Claire Nyquist" description="Sketchbook studies of mosses">
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-8">
    <!-- Back Navigation -->
    <div class="mb-8">
      <a href="/minnesota-bryophytes" class="inline-flex items-center text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800 font-medium">
        ← Back to Minnesota Mosses
      </a>
    </div>

    <!-- Project Header -->
    <div class="text-center mb-12">
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl name-gradient mb-6">
        Mosses Sketchbook
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 max-w-3xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
        This sketch shows the initial concept for the Minnesota Mosses visualization. Initially intended to be 3D printed and cover the world, it was inspired by the work of citizen scientists who post their observations to iNaturalist, the Global Biodiversity Information Facility (GBIF) from where the data comes, and Shane Hope's <em>Public Panopticon Powder</em>, an artwork of 3D printed abstractions of data. Robin Wall Kimmerer's <em>Gathering Moss: A Natural and Cultural History of Mosses</em> also inspired my interest in moss. My Minnesota Mosses visualization is intended to be furry like the plants they represent, with the data growing over the state as moss does.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Featured Image -->
    <div class="mb-12">
      <div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow-lg overflow-hidden hover:shadow-xl transition-all duration-300">
        <div class="relative">
          <img
            src="/images/bryophytasketchbook.jpeg"
            alt="Sketchbook page of handwritten brainstorming notes and pencil diagrams for a moss data sculpture, with green shaded terrain drawings."
            class="w-full h-auto object-contain"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Navigation -->
    <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-gray-200">
      <div class="flex justify-between items-center">
        <a href="/minnesota-bryophytes" class="inline-flex items-center text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800 font-medium">
          ← Back to Minnesota Mosses
        </a>
        <div class="text-sm text-gray-500">
          Sketchbook
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
